WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:04.504
-The President is in a standoff
with Congress

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:06.305
as some Democrats
call for impeachment.

00:00:06.305 --> 00:00:08.374
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:08.374 --> 00:00:12.311
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.311 --> 00:00:14.980
President Trump is defying
subpoenas from Congress.

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:16.249
His attorney general threatened

00:00:16.249 --> 00:00:17.883
not to show up
to hearings this week,

00:00:17.883 --> 00:00:19.786
and several Democrats
have called on Congress

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:21.387
to begin the process
of impeachment.

00:00:21.387 --> 00:00:24.090
So Trump has a lot going on,
which means, of course,

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.292
that he decided to take time
out of his schedule

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:28.728
to call in to a Fox morning show

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:31.397
and once again spent
so much time on the phone

00:00:31.397 --> 00:00:32.698
that at the end
of the interview,

00:00:32.698 --> 00:00:34.967
the host, Maria Bartiromo,

00:00:34.967 --> 00:00:37.536
repeatedly tried to get him
to hang up.

00:00:37.536 --> 00:00:41.975
-Everybody wants people
to go out

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:44.511
and find out
what the hell happened,

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:47.046
where did all
of this corruption start.

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:48.214
When you have --

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:49.982
-Well, certainly our viewers
want to know.

00:00:49.982 --> 00:00:51.184
-The lovers, we call them.

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:52.252
-Yeah, our viewers
want to know that.

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:53.452
-Saying, "We want
an insurance policy."

00:00:53.452 --> 00:00:54.754
-Mr. President,
thank you so much.

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:56.155
-"...Hillary Clinton loses.

00:00:56.155 --> 00:00:59.692
We want an insurance policy
where we can get Trump out."

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:01.160
Well, it didn't work so well.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.762
But I'll tell you what,
it really hurt our country,

00:01:03.762 --> 00:01:05.064
and it hurts our country.

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:06.732
These people are corrupt.
-Yeah.

00:01:06.732 --> 00:01:09.535
-And then you look at a guy
like Brennan with his big mouth.

00:01:09.535 --> 00:01:11.003
But it's a disgrace.

00:01:11.003 --> 00:01:12.338
Everyone wants to know, Maria,

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:14.207
and you might be number one
on the list.

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:16.642
I watch your show.
You're incredible.

00:01:16.642 --> 00:01:18.478
You may be number one
on the list.

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:20.446
Everybody wants to know,
"How did it start?

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:21.647
Why did it start?

00:01:21.647 --> 00:01:23.683
What about the dossier?"
-Well, we want to know.

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:26.285
-How much did Hillary Clinton
pay for the dossier?

00:01:26.285 --> 00:01:27.620
You know she paid for it.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:29.722
You know, everybody
wants to know about it.

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:32.024
And that's really -- Hopefully
they'll be going there.

00:01:32.024 --> 00:01:34.994
-My God, that was like
watching your grandpa

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:37.764
try to get off the phone
with his grandpa.

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:39.999
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:42.301
[ Applause ]

00:01:42.301 --> 00:01:45.004
She ran out of minutes
on her plan.

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:47.640
He's like one of those guys
who calls a restaurant

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.208
to place an order for delivery

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:52.344
and then tries to have
a conversation with the staff.

00:01:52.344 --> 00:01:54.214
"Yeah, I'll take
a large pepperoni,

00:01:54.214 --> 00:01:55.548
and, hey, what's your name?

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:59.018
You always been interested
in pizza?"

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:01.320
I know it's hard
to remember this sometimes,

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:03.890
but that guy is the most
powerful man in the world.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.558
He should be, like, doing stuff.

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:08.328
And Maria knows.
I mean, look at her face.

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:12.598
That's the face you make
when your friend says,

00:02:12.598 --> 00:02:14.166
"I want to set you up
with a guy.

00:02:14.166 --> 00:02:15.168
He's a count."

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:16.569
And then halfway
through the dinner,

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:19.505
you realize she meant
he can count.

00:02:19.505 --> 00:02:20.840
[ As Donald Trump ]
Oh, I know them all.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:24.309
One, two, three.
Can't live without that number.

00:02:24.309 --> 00:02:26.713
[ Normal voice ] But aside
from rambling incoherently

00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:28.514
about whatever
he was rambling about,

00:02:28.514 --> 00:02:30.316
Trump also repeated
the dangerous line

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:32.151
he's been using lately
about the investigation

00:02:32.151 --> 00:02:34.987
of him and his campaign --
that it was an attempted coup

00:02:34.987 --> 00:02:36.990
and the people behind it
were traitors.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:39.025
He used it in the interview
with Bartiromo

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:40.960
and repeated it in speeches
and interviews

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.161
over the last few weeks.

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:44.697
-This was an attempted coup.

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:47.433
This was an attempted takedown
of a president,

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:48.567
and they got caught.

00:02:48.567 --> 00:02:50.636
And what they did was treason.

00:02:50.636 --> 00:02:51.837
This was really a coup attempt.

00:02:51.837 --> 00:02:52.872
-It's all quite extraordinary,
Mr. President.

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:53.872
-It didn't work.
We caught them.

00:02:53.872 --> 00:02:55.741
-Yeah.
-They tried for a coup.

00:02:55.741 --> 00:02:57.276
Didn't work out so well.

00:02:57.276 --> 00:02:58.744
This was a coup.

00:02:58.744 --> 00:03:02.982
This was an attempted overthrow
of the United States government.

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:05.084
-So, there you go.
That's what the President said.

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:06.352
This was a coup,

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:08.154
and the people who
orchestrated it were traitors.

00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:10.189
And of there's anything
Trump hates, it's traitors

00:03:10.189 --> 00:03:13.559
who try to overthrow
the United States government.

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:16.429
-There were very fine people
on both sides.

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:18.263
-Oh, I've answered
that question.

00:03:18.263 --> 00:03:19.932
And if you look at what I said,

00:03:19.932 --> 00:03:23.670
you will see that that question
was answered perfectly.

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:26.338
And I was talking
about people that went

00:03:26.338 --> 00:03:28.474
because they felt very strongly

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:31.877
about the monument to
Robert E. Lee, a great general.

00:03:31.877 --> 00:03:35.247
Whether you like it or not, he
was one of the great generals.

00:03:35.247 --> 00:03:36.915
-First of all, no, he wasn't.

00:03:36.915 --> 00:03:39.218
He led an armed rebellion

00:03:39.218 --> 00:03:41.654
to bring down the United States
government and he lost.

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:43.956
In other words...
-They tried for a coup.

00:03:43.956 --> 00:03:45.725
Didn't work out so well.

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:48.294
-And on top of that --
on top of that --

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:49.829
Can't believe we have to
keep saying this,

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:51.964
but your response to
Charlottesville was not perfect.

00:03:51.964 --> 00:03:54.199
There were no very fine people
on both sides.

00:03:54.199 --> 00:03:56.536
There were literal
white supremacists shouting,

00:03:56.536 --> 00:03:57.904
"Jews will not replace us."

00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:59.438
And they were carrying
tiki torches,

00:03:59.438 --> 00:04:00.973
which is something
we will never forget,

00:04:00.973 --> 00:04:03.743
because now
when you buy a tiki torch,

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:05.410
you have to go out of your way
to say,

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:08.347
"We're having a barbecue!

00:04:08.347 --> 00:04:11.517
It's for barbecue stuff."

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:13.252
But, of course,
Trump couldn't just stop

00:04:13.252 --> 00:04:14.987
at heaping praise
on a traitorous general

00:04:14.987 --> 00:04:16.355
who defended slavery

00:04:16.355 --> 00:04:18.057
and tried to bring down
the United States government.

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:20.359
He also had to heap some praise
on himself.

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:24.797
-Mr. President, how old
is too old to be president?

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:28.634
-Well, I think that
I just feel like a young man.

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:29.968
I'm so young!

00:04:29.968 --> 00:04:32.171
I can't believe it.
I'm the youngest person.

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:35.274
I am a young, vibrant man.

00:04:35.274 --> 00:04:37.009
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.009 --> 00:04:42.482
-I can't believe I have to
say this, but we can see you.

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:44.817
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:45.684
[ Applause ]

00:04:45.684 --> 00:04:48.054
I mean, what are we...

00:04:48.054 --> 00:04:52.724
even supposed to do
with that information?

00:04:52.724 --> 00:04:54.860
That's a 72-year-old
president of the United States,

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:57.363
a man who spends most
of his time watching cable TV

00:04:57.363 --> 00:04:58.764
and riding around in a golf cart

00:04:58.764 --> 00:05:01.200
and stands like he's in
"Weekend at Bernie's."

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:04.470
I mean, here he is
at his golf club recently

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:07.273
with fellow lumpy grandpa
Rush Limbaugh.

00:05:07.273 --> 00:05:08.307
Look at that.

00:05:08.307 --> 00:05:10.109
It's like an episode
of "Star Trek"

00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:13.045
where a transporter malfunction
creates a second Trump.

00:05:13.045 --> 00:05:14.113
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:15.681
And in case defending
Robert E. Lee

00:05:15.681 --> 00:05:17.983
or calling himself a young,
vibrant man wasn't enough,

00:05:17.983 --> 00:05:20.319
Trump also made a bunch
of public appearances where,

00:05:20.319 --> 00:05:22.855
as usual,
sounds came out of his mouth

00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:25.324
that sounded vaguely
like human words.

00:05:25.324 --> 00:05:28.594
-Look, it's a rigged system,
okay?

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:32.932
If I told you how crazy it is,
the web -- It's a web.

00:05:32.932 --> 00:05:36.101
You need 193 IQ
to even understand.

00:05:36.101 --> 00:05:40.406
This web of geniuses, they put
this thing to lower drug price.

00:05:40.406 --> 00:05:43.643
It has 19 effects here and 27.

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:46.045
We got it down, and we're
getting it down further.

00:05:46.045 --> 00:05:47.513
We have the smartest people,

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:49.882
the best people in that world
working on it.

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:55.188
This treaty
threatened your subjugate.

00:05:55.188 --> 00:05:58.157
And you know exactly
what's going on here.

00:05:58.157 --> 00:05:59.592
Your rights.

00:05:59.592 --> 00:06:02.795
I always say this, because
as good as that equipment is --

00:06:02.795 --> 00:06:03.996
and it's genius --

00:06:03.996 --> 00:06:07.667
the greatest equipment
in the world is a dog.

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:12.805
Dogs, a certain type of
German shepherd in particular.

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:18.144
Dogs do a better job than
$400 million worth of equipment.

00:06:18.144 --> 00:06:21.013
-I mean, good Lord, it's like
getting cornered at a party

00:06:21.013 --> 00:06:26.085
by a guy who's almost
run out of cocaine.

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:28.954
"I use a dog, though.
That's what I use."

00:06:28.954 --> 00:06:30.923
The only thing that's impressive
about Trump

00:06:30.923 --> 00:06:32.925
is that the range of subjects
he rambles about

00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:34.293
gets wider and wider every day.

00:06:34.293 --> 00:06:36.328
Most of the time he'll say
the same stuff over and over

00:06:36.328 --> 00:06:38.464
about building a wall
or crooked Hillary or fake news.

00:06:38.464 --> 00:06:39.798
But once in a while
he'll mix in something

00:06:39.798 --> 00:06:42.835
totally bat[bleep] crazy
like smart dogs with high IQs

00:06:42.835 --> 00:06:44.870
or whatever the hell
he was talking about.

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:48.107
Honestly, there's a good chance
someone switched his Fox News

00:06:48.107 --> 00:06:51.043
to an episode of "Wishbone"
and he thought it was real.

00:06:51.043 --> 00:06:53.980
[ As Donald Trump ] You have to
see this dog -- so smart.

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:57.850
Solving mysteries.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:07:00.953
[ Normal voice ] Also -- Also...

00:07:00.953 --> 00:07:04.089
can we...

00:07:04.089 --> 00:07:06.458
can we hear the crowd reaction
to that line?

00:07:06.458 --> 00:07:09.828
-The greatest equipment
in the world is a dog.

00:07:09.828 --> 00:07:11.830
Dogs...
[ Scattered applause ]

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:14.700
...a certain type of
German shepherd in particular.

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:17.536
-The weirdest thing
about being at a Trump speech

00:07:17.536 --> 00:07:19.738
is those moments you have to
hesitantly clap

00:07:19.738 --> 00:07:22.141
for stuff you know
you don't understand.

00:07:22.141 --> 00:07:25.711
"Yeah, dogs.

00:07:25.711 --> 00:07:28.714
Yeah, the best equipment's
a dog, right?

00:07:28.714 --> 00:07:31.017
We didn't elect
a [bleep] maniac, right?

00:07:31.017 --> 00:07:34.120
Yeah. Yeah.

00:07:36.455 --> 00:07:38.157
Yeah."

00:07:38.157 --> 00:07:40.459
As all this dumb stuff
keeps happening,

00:07:40.459 --> 00:07:41.760
it's impossible to remember

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:43.895
that Special Counsel
Robert Mueller's final report

00:07:43.895 --> 00:07:45.498
came out
less than two weeks ago,

00:07:45.498 --> 00:07:48.801
and it confirmed much of what we
already suspected about Trump,

00:07:48.801 --> 00:07:50.269
including the fact
that he and his team

00:07:50.269 --> 00:07:51.971
openly welcomed
the help of Russians

00:07:51.971 --> 00:07:53.673
seeking to interfere
in the election

00:07:53.673 --> 00:07:54.973
and repeatedly lied about it

00:07:54.973 --> 00:07:56.608
and tried to interfere
in the investigation of it.

00:07:56.608 --> 00:07:58.176
We've basically known that
for two years,

00:07:58.176 --> 00:08:01.013
but now we have
a 400-page report to prove it.

00:08:01.013 --> 00:08:03.983
I mean, even the page count
looks bad for Trump.

00:08:03.983 --> 00:08:06.085
If you hired a private detective

00:08:06.085 --> 00:08:07.953
to find out if your wife
is cheating

00:08:07.953 --> 00:08:12.024
and he sent you 400 pages,
you wouldn't even read them.

00:08:12.024 --> 00:08:14.126
You'd go straight
to your lawyer's office.

00:08:14.126 --> 00:08:18.931
Like, "Chad has
his own section!"

00:08:18.931 --> 00:08:22.768
And let's remember the report
specifically listed 10 times

00:08:22.768 --> 00:08:24.437
Trump may have
obstructed justice.

00:08:24.437 --> 00:08:27.273
And Mueller's team even went out
of their way to say explicitly

00:08:27.273 --> 00:08:28.808
that they could not
exonerate them.

00:08:28.808 --> 00:08:31.677
Instead, Mueller specifically
turned it over to Congress.

00:08:31.677 --> 00:08:33.112
-While Mueller stopped short

00:08:33.112 --> 00:08:35.047
of taking a position
on obstruction,

00:08:35.047 --> 00:08:38.250
his words suggest Congress
now has a role to play.

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:41.453
He writes, "We concluded
that Congress has authority

00:08:41.453 --> 00:08:44.223
to prohibit a president's
corrupt use of his authority

00:08:44.223 --> 00:08:46.191
in order to protect
the integrity

00:08:46.191 --> 00:08:47.960
of the administration
of justice."

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:49.395
-This is from
the Mueller report.

00:08:49.395 --> 00:08:52.765
The conclusion that Congress
may apply the obstruction laws

00:08:52.765 --> 00:08:56.201
to the President's corrupt
exercise of the powers of office

00:08:56.201 --> 00:08:59.705
accords with our constitutional
system of checks and balances

00:08:59.705 --> 00:09:02.708
and the principle that no person
is above the law.

00:09:02.708 --> 00:09:04.409
-It's amazing Trump
and his supporters

00:09:04.409 --> 00:09:06.145
are celebrating this
as an exoneration

00:09:06.145 --> 00:09:08.647
when Mueller keeps hinting
that Congress could take actions

00:09:08.647 --> 00:09:10.182
that were unavailable
to Mueller.

00:09:10.182 --> 00:09:14.753
For example, in Footnote 574,
Appendix B, Subsection 48C,

00:09:14.753 --> 00:09:16.922
Mueller writes...
[Coughing] impeachment.

00:09:16.922 --> 00:09:19.391
[ Laughter ]

00:09:19.391 --> 00:09:22.327
The facts couldn't have been
any clearer in Mueller's report.

00:09:22.327 --> 00:09:23.628
Congress has the authority

00:09:23.628 --> 00:09:25.965
to investigate Trump
for obstruction of justice

00:09:25.965 --> 00:09:27.366
and hold him accountable for it.

00:09:27.366 --> 00:09:28.834
This is why we have
a Congress --

00:09:28.834 --> 00:09:30.135
to reign in a lawless president.

00:09:30.135 --> 00:09:31.636
You have all the evidence
you need.

00:09:31.636 --> 00:09:34.139
But if you still want to find
more evidence, just remember...

00:09:34.139 --> 00:09:37.275
-The greatest equipment
in the world is a dog.

00:09:37.275 --> 00:09:39.111
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:09:39.111 --> 00:09:41.380
[ Cheers and applause ]

